  "limitations": [
    "Effective hours are hours after training/absence/skill constraints, not gross hires or job postings. Hiring must lead output; no observed training lag is fitted.",
    "Original output and hours at Q3 are residual/proxy allocations, not measured site production or contemporaneous hours. OSHA hours include multiple roles; FTE equivalents are not technician counts.",
    "10% is a working sensitivity, not estimated from two tours. 5/15% bracket execution; no rate is calibrated to consensus.",
    "Existing ADESA cohorts remain at earlier 13k standard capacity; further staffing headroom there is unquantified.",
    "Capacity is potential, not guaranteed demand. Growth needs inventory sourcing and profitable sales absorption. No new demand forecast is supplied.",
    "Incremental normal direct labor is already inside unit gross profit: memo only; do not subtract twice. SG&A, capex and WC use previous provisional assumptions; no revised EBITDA or target price is claimed.",
    "Physical line/equipment expansion needs separate capex; staffing-only plan does not fund new line installation.",
    "Marginal SG&A inherits a companywide retail-volume cost driver even though wholesale units are held at consensus; a segment-specific cost split remains necessary.",
    "No standalone historical-gap recovery is added: the new original-network path replaces that calculation.",
    "Monthly midpoint averaging is numerical approximation; seasonality is not modeled.",
    "Post-cap productivity case allows fewer hours at constant output; that is an efficiency scenario, not a layoff forecast."
  ],
